tant balancing process will anchor the stablecoin around its $1 target while maintaining system safety. A target to 400% The Mutuum Finance (MUTM) development team will deliver its Version 1 rollout through the Sepolia Testnet in Q4 2025. The early release will feature lending pools, mtTokens, debt tokens, and the automated liquidator bot — initially supporting ETH and USDT for collateral and borrowing. Later on, this beta testing phase will align with expected exchange listings, giving users real access to platform features and marking the first major utility wave for MUTM tokens. Analysts projecting a 400% price increase emphasize four core growth drivers supporting Mutuum Finance (MUTM). The first is its Reserve Factor, which redirects a portion of borrower interest into the protocol’s reserves. This feature will act as an on-chain safety buffer, strengthening solvency and supporting long-term value creation linked to future governance and token utilities. The second is its Deposit and Borrow Caps. These limits will protect the system from overexposure to volatile assets, creating trust among larger investors. By controlling capital inflows responsibly, Mutuum Finance (MUTM) will attract more institutional liquidity post-launch, indirectly boosting demand for MUTM. The third catalyst lies in Enhanced Collateral Efficiency. Correlated and low-volatility assets like stablecoins will enjoy higher borrowing limits. This improvement increases total lending volume, generating more interest income, which in turn funds MUTM buybacks and mtToken staking rewards. Finally, upcoming exchange listings are expected to expand accessibility and liquidity worldwide. These listings will expose MUTM to a broader audience and accelerate volume growth, giving it the visibility needed to sustain a steady upward trajectory. A simple numerical projection underscores how early investors benefit. A Phase 2 participant who invested $1,500 at $0.015 now holds tokens valued more than $3,500 